## Codex-specific rules (each one cost real sessions; evidence in synthesis/2026-08-04-codex-vs-claude.md)

- **Conventions are not auto-loaded here.** If the repo has CLAUDE.md (or similar conventions
  file), READ IT NOW — and if AGENTS.md doesn't exist, create it as a one-line pointer to
  CLAUDE.md and commit it, so future Codex sessions load conventions automatically.
- **Every shell call is a fresh shell.** `cd`, `export`, `$!`, and `mktemp` outputs do not
  survive between calls. Name working dirs deterministically (`/private/tmp/<slug>-<date>`)
  in a single call; never let a generated path be the only record of itself.
- **Approvals are session state.** Append every granted approval to a running decision log
  (scratch file or PR comment) the moment it's given; grep it BEFORE asking any approval
  question. A rejected write is a transport/credential fact until proven a consent fact —
  check the token/remote before asking the human for permission they already gave.
- **Latest instruction wins.** When a new instruction conflicts with a standing one, follow
  the newer and say which rule you're dropping. When blocked by a standing prohibition, name
  the exact phrase that lifts it ("reply 'merge approved' to lift the no-merge rule").
- **Never re-issue a byte-identical command.** Before re-running, state what changed since
  the last run; if nothing changed, the previous result is the result.
